{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793372065,"nonce":"qp+aYcFGRTJtd4d4NKkTfuS9lyM=","title":"Display-list replay for OpenFL and Flixel: serialize the scene and draw it with Ashui's DrawContext","message":"Later optimization to the pixel surface for frameworks with a retained display list. The producer sends scene deltas (display objects, transforms, Graphics commands, bitmaps as resources by id, text with fonts) and RayDE replays them with DrawContext (paths, text, image, clips, transforms), so bandwidth is small and the picture is resolution independent. Limits to settle first: filters, blend modes, masks, shaders and Stage3D fall back to the pixel surface; fonts and text metrics must match the app's. Only worth building if the pixel surface measurements in the transport issue show the bandwidth is a problem.\n\nPart of the framework previews epic: git-bug 9c6f60e27c2cb4be92d534eccc95910e303a5c4e03e1e8779c6d52ca9c40a330","files":null}]}